Local quick-start

App stack:

```bash
cd /Users/manzil/spe
docker compose up --build
```

Main endpoints:

- frontend: http://localhost:3000
- backend: http://localhost:8081
- ml-model: http://localhost:8000

ELK stack:

```bash
cd /Users/manzil/spe
docker compose -f observability/docker-compose.elk.yml up -d
```

Observability endpoints:

- Elasticsearch: http://localhost:9200
- Kibana: http://localhost:5601

Kubernetes apply order:

```bash
kubectl apply -f k8s/namespace.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/ml-model.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/backend.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/frontend.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/hpa.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/fluent-bit.yaml
```

Useful checks:

```bash
kubectl get all -n medical-chatbot
kubectl get hpa -n medical-chatbot
kubectl top pods -n medical-chatbot
```

Vault setup for compose deploy:

```bash
export VAULT_TOKEN=your-token
export VAULT_DEV_ROOT_TOKEN_ID="$VAULT_TOKEN"
docker compose -f security/docker-compose.vault.yml up -d
vault kv put secret/medical-chatbot \
  ml_service_url="http://ml-model:8000/predict" \
  backend_shared_secret="your-shared-secret"
```

Jenkins pipeline:

- webhook-triggered from GitHub
- supports `compose` and `kubernetes` deploy targets
- builds immutable image tags using commit SHA
- scans images with Trivy
- verifies deployment after rollout
- expects a Jenkins secret text credential named `vault-token` for compose deployments
- compose deploys inside Jenkins reach Vault via `http://host.docker.internal:8200`
